# HubHex API — tests locaux (extension REST Client dans VS Code / Cursor)
# 1. Installer l'extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client)
# 2. cd backend && npm run dev
# 3. Ouvrir ce fichier, cliquer "Send Request" au-dessus de chaque requete

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@email = test@example.com
@password = MotDePasse1
@username = testuser
@token = 
@refreshToken = 

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Register (une fois)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Login — copier token et refreshToken dans les variables ci-dessus
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Refresh (nouveau access + refresh, rotation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Logout (invalide le refresh)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Profil (connecte)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### PATCH pseudo + statut
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "display_name": "Mon Pseudo",
  "status_emoji": "🚀",
  "status_message": "Test REST Client"
}

### Dashboard
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard?activityLimit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Projets publics
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/community/projects?sort=recent
